<title>FRANCE: Schneider says Spie sale neutral.</title>
<headline>Schneider says Spie sale neutral.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French electrical equipment company Schneider said on Friday the one billion franc sale of its Spie Batignolles construction company to Britain's Amec Plc and Spie's employees would not have a significant impact on its accounts.</p>
<p>&quot;The transaction will not have a significant impact on our accounts. The value is very close to the net value of Spie Batignolles and Spie Trindel on our books,&quot; Jean-Claude Perrin, Schneider finance director said.</p>
<p>However he did confirm a forecast for a higher net attributable profit for the grou in 1996.</p>
</text>
